  "title": "The Kite That Rebuilt the Skyline",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "block-world chain reactions",
  "premise": "A cubic festival organizer must raise a skyline-shaped banner, but the folded display lies in a heap. A tethered fantasy kite pulls a guided cable through successive counterweighted facades, raising each panel to its stop until their shadows spell the festival’s invented name.",
  "hook": "The skyline is packed flat. The kite is clocking in.",
  "visible_action": "Kite climbs on a fixed path; cable runs through visible guides; facades pivot upright in sequence; their shadows align into letters.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "The order of assembly can be part of the spectacle.",
  "gate": "Toy fantasy kite and architecture; no real rigging, aviation, or load-bearing instruction.",
